  run_ids: ["ab9062bb-e262-4810-949c-bdb307676a8e"] -> ["a2c0ecdb-0fee-409e-8f45-0eea3045f341"]
  explanation: "For nohash-hasher 0.2.0 on x86_64 with std enabled or disabled, Default initializes the stored value to zero, Clone preserves state, and finish returns the stored integer. Each of the ten integer write methods stores the Rust conversion of its input to u64: unsigned values are widened and signed values are converted modulo 2^64. With debug assertions enabled, the first integer write succeeds and a later write fails its assertion. With debug assertions disabled, each integer write replaces the stored value. The generic byte-slice write always panics in both configurations. These are exact per-method state and result contracts over all inputs, proved from unchanged published Rust bodies. Separate original-body Kani evidence checks handwritten Debug::fmt for NoHashHasher<u8> after Default or one arbitrary write_u8, using default {:?} formatting into a fixed 64-byte writer. Successful output has exact tuple delimiters, canonical decimal state and, in debug mode, the correct written flag. A writer that errors on its first call propagates Err and leaves its buffer unchanged. All std/no_std dependency and debug/release combinations pass separately: 2175 debug and 2143 release checks in each feature configuration; the verification harness itself uses std. This is a bounded formatter/input-domain supplement, not another Aeneas API claim or a proof for arbitrary stored u64 values, writers, formatting options or partial-write failures. A separate Kani supplement executes the actual standard Clone::clone_from default body and original manual Clone for NoHashHasher<u64>, in all four configurations. Source and destination independently begin at Default or one arbitrary write_u64. Public finish checks destination replacement and source preservation; a distinct full-original-prefix fixture with read-only getters also checks the debug written flag. The eight jobs succeed (public-value stage 47 debug or 28 release checks, flag-observer stage 104 or 81 checks per feature configuration). This concrete reachable-state Rust-body guarantee is separate from the generic Lean composition through the official default model; arbitrary T, other std revisions and other state histories remain unproved. Separate generic Lean contracts cover actual public Hasher::write_length_prefix, write_u128 and write_i128 calls through compiler-inlined UFCS callers in std/no_std with debug assertions enabled/disabled. For every represented T under the original IsEnabled bound and every receiver state, debug length-prefix stores the usize-to-u64 cast and marks written when previously unwritten, or fails assertionFailure when already written. Without debug assertions it always overwrites the stored word. Both wide integer calls fail panic for every input and receiver state because their original standard defaults reach NoHashHasher::write. The separate900-check Kani evidence covers the ten original integer T instantiations: debug initial states and release default-or-once-written public states." -> "For nohash-hasher 0.2.0 on x86_64 with std enabled or disabled, Default initializes the stored value to zero, Clone preserves state, and finish returns the stored integer. Each of the ten integer write methods stores the Rust conversion of its input to u64: unsigned values are widened and signed values are converted modulo 2^64. With debug assertions enabled, the first integer write succeeds and a later write fails its assertion. With debug assertions disabled, each integer write replaces the stored value. The generic byte-slice write always panics in both configurations. These are exact per-method state and result contracts over all inputs, proved from unchanged published Rust bodies. Separate original-body Kani evidence checks handwritten Debug::fmt for NoHashHasher<u8> after Default or one arbitrary write_u8, using default {:?} formatting into a fixed 64-byte writer. Successful output has exact tuple delimiters, canonical decimal state and, in debug mode, the correct written flag. A writer that errors on its first call propagates Err and leaves its buffer unchanged. All std/no_std dependency and debug/release combinations pass separately: 2175 debug and 2143 release checks in each feature configuration; the verification harness itself uses std. This is a bounded formatter/input-domain supplement, not another Aeneas API claim or a proof for arbitrary stored u64 values, writers, formatting options or partial-write failures. A separate Kani supplement executes the actual standard Clone::clone_from default body and original manual Clone for NoHashHasher<u64>, in all four configurations. Source and destination independently begin at Default or one arbitrary write_u64. Public finish checks destination replacement and source preservation; a distinct full-original-prefix fixture with read-only getters also checks the debug written flag. The eight jobs succeed (public-value stage 47 debug or 28 release checks, flag-observer stage 104 or 81 checks per feature configuration). This concrete reachable-state Rust-body guarantee is separate from the generic Lean composition through the official default model; arbitrary T, other std revisions and other state histories remain unproved. Separate generic Lean contracts cover actual public Hasher::write_length_prefix, write_u128 and write_i128 calls through compiler-inlined UFCS callers in std/no_std with debug assertions enabled/disabled. For every represented T under the original IsEnabled bound and every receiver state, debug length-prefix stores the usize-to-u64 cast and marks written when previously unwritten, or fails assertionFailure when already written. Without debug assertions it always overwrites the stored word. Both wide integer calls fail panic for every input and receiver state because their original standard defaults reach NoHashHasher::write. The separate900-check Kani evidence covers the ten original integer T instantiations: debug initial states and release default-or-once-written public states. Four further generic compiler-inlined caller contracts cover original Hasher::write_str in std/no_std with debug assertions enabled/disabled. For every represented T under IsEnabled, receiver state and string, including empty strings, the call fails panic: the original default first calls NoHashHasher::write on the string bytes, which unconditionally panics, so the trailing write_u8(0xff) is unreachable. There is no fixed string-length/content restriction."
  trusted_assumptions: "The Rust compiler, Charon/Aeneas translation, their standard-library models, and the Lean kernel are trusted. The checked theorems use no extra local axioms; their transitive dependencies are limited to Lean's propext, Classical.choice, and Quot.sound. Generic inherited-call proofs additionally trust the pinned Rust optimized MIR compiler Inline pass and, for wide calls, SimplifyLocals-final dead-code elimination before official Charon/Aeneas extraction. The caller/stdlib/original-method source guards and configuration layouts are retained. This is not a compiler-correctness or direct default-declaration source-card proof; no source/LLBC/generated edits, new model or panic stub is introduced." -> "The Rust compiler, Charon/Aeneas translation, their standard-library models, and the Lean kernel are trusted. The checked theorems use no extra local axioms; their transitive dependencies are limited to Lean's propext, Classical.choice, and Quot.sound. Generic inherited-call proofs additionally trust the pinned Rust optimized MIR compiler Inline pass and, for wide calls, SimplifyLocals-final dead-code elimination before official Charon/Aeneas extraction. The caller/stdlib/original-method source guards and configuration layouts are retained. This is not a compiler-correctness or direct default-declaration source-card proof; no source/LLBC/generated edits, new model or panic stub is introduced. write_str additionally uses the pinned official rustc Inline, RemoveStorageMarkers, ReferencePropagation, DeadStoreElimination-final and SimplifyLocals-final passes through optimized MIR/official Charon and unchanged Aeneas. Source/IR guards connect the actual UFCS caller, standard default and original panic source spans. The final generated body does not read the string or call another function. This trusts compiler inlining/cleanup, not a compiler-correctness proof, panic stub or direct default-method API-card binding."
  environment: "Unmodified crates.io nohash-hasher 0.2.0; x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, std enabled and disabled; debug_assertions true and false. Charon 08d7c9d50144bd84848212c24701253585e90d1f, Aeneas be86ab0f1989d04944292b345b24c435be3ad10a, Rust nightly-2026-09-17, Lean 4.35.0. Official start-from roots select the actual method bodies; the official namespace option separates debug/release translations. Fourteen public theorems each conjoin all four std/no-std and debug/release configurations. The supplementary clone_from composition is included in the fresh Lean build without adding an API mapping. cargo-proofs 0.4.1 has the documented TLS-CA and upstream audit-variable compatibility fixes; the allowed-axiom policy is unchanged. Added evidence/hasher-inherited-family preserves generic3API across four configurations (twelve contracts plus one helper), and separate900 Kani checks with zero failures. Generic extraction uses pinned September compiler/official frontend with Inline/DCE; Kani uses its separately pinned August compiler. Import-only integration connects HasherFamilyAudit to the configured primary Proofs module, so the actual CLI targets must print all13 supplemental axiom audits. All old14 mappings and preconditions remain unchanged." -> "Unmodified crates.io nohash-hasher 0.2.0; x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, std enabled and disabled; debug_assertions true and false. Charon 08d7c9d50144bd84848212c24701253585e90d1f, Aeneas be86ab0f1989d04944292b345b24c435be3ad10a, Rust nightly-2026-09-17, Lean 4.35.0. Official start-from roots select the actual method bodies; the official namespace option separates debug/release translations. Fourteen public theorems each conjoin all four std/no-std and debug/release configurations. The supplementary clone_from composition is included in the fresh Lean build without adding an API mapping. cargo-proofs 0.4.1 has the documented TLS-CA and upstream audit-variable compatibility fixes; the allowed-axiom policy is unchanged. Added evidence/hasher-inherited-family preserves generic3API across four configurations (twelve contracts plus one helper), and separate900 Kani checks with zero failures. Generic extraction uses pinned September compiler/official frontend with Inline/DCE; Kani uses its separately pinned August compiler. Import-only integration connects HasherFamilyAudit to the configured primary Proofs module, so the actual CLI targets must print all13 supplemental axiom audits. All old14 mappings and preconditions remain unchanged. evidence/write-str-inline4 preserves the new103-file frozen packet and source/type/evidence reviews. Existing HasherFamilyAudit imports the four new proof modules and audits17 unique supplementary declarations (old13 plus new4); the actual +Proofs CLI target must include all17 markers. Original14 mappings and all prior13/900 evidence remain preserved."
  evidence_url: "https://github.com/nyuichi/rust-crate-proofs/tree/febb64d951fae5cf240ac2951aa5821f68da2511" -> "https://github.com/nyuichi/rust-crate-proofs/tree/9db263d0e4a64a25b8d39b54837ad0e64b827ce3"
  limitations: "Coverage consists of Default, Clone, ten integer writers, write, and finish in the stated debug/release configurations. General Debug behavior beyond the separate u8/default-format/fixed-writer Kani domain, other inherited Hasher default methods beyond the three supplemental actual-caller contracts described here, full trait-instance integration, custom Hash implementations, BuildHasherDefault, and HashMap/HashSet behavior are not verified. In particular, this does not establish that a custom IsEnabled type obeys the required single-integer-write Hash protocol. Other targets were not checked. The upstream no-std IsEnabled doctest refers to the std-only IntMap alias and does not compile; the no-std unit tests and proved method bodies pass. A supplementary clone_from theorem composes the actual clone body with the official standard-library default model and proves exact replacement by source; it is not an independent std-body proof or a separate published API claim. write_length_prefix is the pinned nightly hasher_prefixfree_extras API, not a stable-interface guarantee. The new inherited-family results are supplemental actual-caller contracts, not new registered machine API claims; primary coverage stays14. The generic contracts distinguish debug and release receiver layouts and retain IsEnabled/trait correspondence assumptions. Panic messages, unwinding, global effects, other targets/profiles and const evaluation are not established. Kani900 has narrower concrete-T/reachable-state domains and is not a premise of the generic Lean proofs. The producer consolidated regeneration script was not rerun; earlier successful individual extractions/source guards and complete kernel audits are retained, and the formal recorded build recompiles all13 supplemental declarations. The producer READY compiled_sidecars0 flag was inaccurate; twenty listed compiler sidecars are excluded from this public source subset, with an exact erratum list." -> "Coverage consists of Default, Clone, ten integer writers, write, and finish in the stated debug/release configurations. General Debug behavior beyond the separate u8/default-format/fixed-writer Kani domain, other inherited Hasher default methods beyond the four supplemental actual-caller API families described here, full trait-instance integration, custom Hash implementations, BuildHasherDefault, and HashMap/HashSet behavior are not verified. In particular, this does not establish that a custom IsEnabled type obeys the required single-integer-write Hash protocol. Other targets were not checked. The upstream no-std IsEnabled doctest refers to the std-only IntMap alias and does not compile; the no-std unit tests and proved method bodies pass. A supplementary clone_from theorem composes the actual clone body with the official standard-library default model and proves exact replacement by source; it is not an independent std-body proof or a separate published API claim. write_length_prefix is the pinned nightly hasher_prefixfree_extras API, not a stable-interface guarantee. The new inherited-family results are supplemental actual-caller contracts, not new registered machine API claims; primary coverage stays14. The generic contracts distinguish debug and release receiver layouts and retain IsEnabled/trait correspondence assumptions. Panic messages, unwinding, global effects, other targets/profiles and const evaluation are not established. Kani900 has narrower concrete-T/reachable-state domains and is not a premise of the generic Lean proofs. The producer consolidated regeneration script was not rerun; earlier successful individual extractions/source guards and complete kernel audits are retained, and the formal recorded build recompiles all13 supplemental declarations. The producer READY compiled_sidecars0 flag was inaccurate; twenty listed compiler sidecars are excluded from this public source subset, with an exact erratum list. write_str is also a pinned nightly hasher_prefixfree_extras API, not a stable-interface guarantee. Its producer READY zero-sidecar flag was inaccurate: sixteen listed compiler sidecars are excluded from this public87-file source subset, with exact hashes and an erratum retained. The write_str results remain supplemental actual-caller contracts with no new registered API claims. Modeled fail panic does not specify panic hooks, messages/locations, unwind/global effects or independent physical memory/alias/lifetime guarantees. Other targets/compiler settings and const evaluation are outside scope. Initial dead TwoPhaseMut-copy translation failures remain historical; the intermediate failing LLBC was not separately frozen before official re-extraction. No source, LLBC or generated body was hand edited. Consolidated portable regeneration/replay has not been run; individual generation, proof and coimport successes are retained."
